# Rust workspace

Generated from {{ template.name }} {{ template.version }}: a Cargo workspace, no Node toolchain.
Crates live in `crates/*`; versions, lints and profiles are set in the root `Cargo.toml`.

## Commands

The CI steps, in order (run them all before saying a change is done):

```bash
cargo fmt --all --check
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings
node scripts/deny.mjs --locked check bans licenses sources
cargo nextest run --workspace --locked --profile ci
cargo test --workspace --doc --locked
```

Also: `cargo fmt --all` (format), `cargo nextest run -p <crate>` (one crate),
`node scripts/agents-index.mjs` (regenerate `docs/agents/index.md`; CI checks it),
`node scripts/licenses.mjs` (regenerate `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md` after dependency changes; CI checks it).
`scripts/ci-extra.sh` (seed): repo checks, run last by CI; keep it fast.

## Rules

- Test first: failing test, then implement; verify with real output before saying a task is done.
- One task per change; small focused files; no drive-by refactors; docs-only PRs need no changelog/progress fragment.
- Dependencies are exact pins (`=x.y.z`); `--locked` everywhere; no `unsafe` (workspace lint).
- Template-owned files (configs, workflows, `.claude/`) change via `splice update --all`; local changes go
  in seed files, `docs/agents/project.md` or a crate's `AGENTS.md`.
- Never print, read or commit secrets (`.env*`, keys). Releases are tag pushes by a human: never publish,
  push tags or push the default branch; open a PR and `gh pr merge --auto`.
- Guard hook: a rail, not a sandbox; real fix: a server-side branch ruleset. See `docs/agents/guard.md`.
- A hook `ask` is a denial in unattended runs: use the alternative its reason names.
- At most 2-3 parallel agents on barely overlapping files; note next steps in `docs/agents/project.md`
  before a long task.

## Crates

{% if no_placeholder %}{% else %}- `crates/common`: shared library code (seed, unpublished). Template tests (crates/common, its test)
  are removable in the bootstrap PR: `git rm -r crates/common`, then `cargo generate-lockfile`.
{% endif %}{% if "rust-cli" in pieces %}- `crates/*` (rust-cli): distributable CLI skeleton with one JSON object on `--json`, fixed exit
  codes and cargo-deny; see `crates/<name>/AGENTS.md`.
{% endif %}
## Where to look

- `docs/agents/project.md`: repo-specific notes; read first.
- `docs/agents/index.md`: generated map of commands, crates and docs.
- `<dir>/AGENTS.md`: notes for one crate.
